    <exercise number="31" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>What do your results in the preceding exercise indicate about the two-sided limit $$\underset{x\rightarrow 1}{\lim }f(x)?$$ Explain your response.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$limx\to 1f(x)limx\to 1f(x)$$ does not exist because $$limx\to 1-f(x)=-2\ne limx\to 1+f(x)=2.limx\to 1-f(x)=-2\ne limx\to 1+f(x)=2.$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
